      "rationale": "This is the non-positive base equation that makes the mathematical factorial summary total; it defines factorial rather than adding an independent fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-061c723304f7123e51ae42344edc69b86c8037ca6606ef3145658939fb695c6b",
      "start_line": 9,
      "text": "  rule factorial(N:Int) => 1\n       requires N <=Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 12,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "458409c7bc07693a15b8bbc9bc5f73e395714f67d4b55f228b0496515b94136f",
      "rationale": "This is the positive-input recurrence defining the mathematical factorial summary in terms of its predecessor.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-458409c7bc07693a15b8bbc9bc5f73e395714f67d4b55f228b0496515b94136f",
      "start_line": 11,
      "text": "  rule factorial(N:Int) => factorial(N -Int 1) *Int N\n       requires N >Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 17,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "edc55d2e0a1a07541a0d8f6c1255456689844a9679ab6259bceb68f8c6465dbe",
      "rationale": "This is the non-positive base equation that makes the specialFactorial mathematical summary total.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-edc55d2e0a1a07541a0d8f6c1255456689844a9679ab6259bceb68f8c6465dbe",
      "start_line": 16,
      "text": "  rule specialFactorial(N:Int) => 1\n       requires N <=Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 20,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "0e4e7b60244adfbc0ed7ab152432bbfd95134e586f60ecb865844be14801286a",
      "rationale": "This recurrence defines specialFactorial as the predecessor product multiplied by the factorial summary at the current positive input.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-0e4e7b60244adfbc0ed7ab152432bbfd95134e586f60ecb865844be14801286a",
      "start_line": 18,
      "text": "  rule specialFactorial(N:Int)\n    => specialFactorial(N -Int 1) *Int factorial(N)\n       requires N >Int 0"
    }
  ],
